  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food insecurity resilience building project through community-based irrigation in Kaarta/Sefeto, Kita Region in Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is to contribute to food self-sufficiency and poverty reduction. It aims at the following specific objectives: (i) Increase production and productivity through the creation of 1017 ha of local Hydro-Agricultural Development (AHA) (20 AHA of lowlands and 33 AHA of small market garden areas); (ii) Improve access to drinking water in the project intervention area through the construction of 27 Improved Village Hydraulic System (SHVA); (iii) Protect 200 ha agricultural land through soil conservation measures (iv) Acquire inputs for fish farming</narrative>
  </description>
